extraction_notes: "THE P.B. CAP IS NOT STORED AS A REQUIREMENT. The book prints ''a P.B. of 12 or lower (they want average looking people)'', which is a MAXIMUM, and attribute_requirements holds minimums only - it is combined with Math.max and rendered as ''PB 12+''. Writing it there would state the exact inverse of the book, silently. See BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F32. It is in restrictions instead, where a player and a GM both see it. Money: the book gives a monthly salary of 4,200-6,000 credits depending on level and skill and says the character starts with one month''s pay; starting_money holds the LOW end, 4200, per the catalog''s range convention. A modest expense account is often provided and is not a stored figure. The book adds that SQ agents get full medical care and access to SQ computers and facilities but are responsible for their own housing. The +1D4 to M.A. is not in bonuses.attributes, which takes a fixed number; the +1 to P.P. is. See extraction note in the Lore section."
---

## Lore

The undercover agents of le Surete du Quebec assume a passive role: watching,
listening and reporting what they see and hear. Two thirds are on assignment
outside of Free Quebec, deep within enemy territory, including the Coalition
States and, to a much lesser degree, even the CS Military.

Excluding informers and sympathizers, most SQ operatives are the equivalent of
the Coalition Law Enforcement Officers of Coalition War Campaign. The Deep Intel
Agents are 40% of the force; ISS Peacekeepers are 10%, ISS Specters 15%, ISS
Intel Specters 20%, and the remaining 15% are mostly administration and
communications. ISS Intel Specters may also engage in this type of duty.

The SQ wants people who do not stand out, which is why the class caps beauty
rather than requiring it. A high M.E. and P.P. are helpful but not necessary.

Standard equipment varies dramatically with the assignment, and the armor is
usually **not** a Quebec type, for obvious reasons. On special assignment an
agent draws surveillance, listening and recording equipment, special optics, a
portable laboratory, still and video cameras, long-range radio, additional
weapons and ammunition, a vehicle, fake documents and similar spy equipment.

## GM Notes

Average level of experience for an NPC agent is 1D4+2.

**The +1D4 to M.A. is rolled at creation and is not applied by the sheet.** The
book''s O.C.C. bonus line reads "+1D4 to M.A. and +1 to P.P. attribute". The +1
to P.P. is stored in `bonuses.attributes` and applies; the +1D4 cannot be, since
that block takes a fixed number rather than a dice expression. Roll it and add
it by hand at creation.

The agent typically holds a job or position within whatever environment they
have infiltrated, and many have families.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'fq-deep-intel-agent');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
